cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PEDRO, please cite it as below."
title: "PEDRO: potential and total energy distributions from Cartesian Hessians, including molecules embedded in large QM/MM models"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Michael Raymond"
    family-names: "Nelson"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-9809-9842"
version: "0.2.0b1"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Fisicas/PEDRO"
abstract: >-
  PEDRO assigns harmonic vibrational modes of molecules embedded in large ONIOM and QM/MM models using
  internal-coordinate total energy distributions (TED), retaining the full model's coupling to its environment.
  It reads Gaussian logs and formatted checkpoints, ORCA Hessian files, VEDA
  input files and a documented program-independent format; describes a molecule embedded in a large QM/MM (ONIOM)
  or partial Hessian in that molecule's own internal coordinates, with the environment's share in the same budget;
  and optionally reads Gaussian GVPT2 overtones, combination bands and resonances with quality checks.
  Isolated-molecule PED/TED are compared against VEDA 4 on identical input. This is a public beta.
keywords:
  - vibrational spectroscopy
  - potential energy distribution
  - total energy distribution
  - normal mode analysis
  - internal coordinates
  - QM/MM
  - ONIOM
  - GVPT2
  - Fermi resonance
  - infrared spectroscopy
